## 2. Modified third-party code — LGPL-3.0

### `tools/solver-patches/`

The Fortran solver in `tools/solver-patches/` is derived from:

> **Image_Velocimetry_Solver**
> INRAE / IRSTEA, France
> https://forge.irstea.fr/projects/lspiv-solver
> Licensed under the **GNU Lesser General Public License v3.0**

**This is a modified version.** We changed 4 of the 33 source files. In accordance with
LGPL-3.0 §4 (Combined Works) and §6, we state the changes explicitly:

| File | Nature of change |
|---|---|
| `sub_PIV.f90` | Added an auto-detecting P5/P2 PGM reader; fixed two uninitialised-variable defects |
| `sub_transf_23D.f90` | Added an auto-detecting P5/P2 PGM reader |
| `transf_23D.f90` | Repointed the image-reader function pointer to the new reader |
| `sub_lspiv_parameter.f90` | Changed the parameter file open mode from read-only to read-write |

The **unmodified originals** of those 4 files are preserved in
`tools/solver-patches/upstream-original/` so the diff can be reconstructed at any time.

Full license texts: `tools/solver-patches/LICENSE.upstream` (LGPL-3.0),
`tools/solver-patches/COPYING.LGPL`, `tools/solver-patches/COPYING.GPL`.

`tools/arm/makefile` carries the same upstream header. It stays under that
solver license grant. The root `LICENSE` covers the original work in section 1.

`kdtree2.f90` carries a separate notice: copyright Matthew Kennel (2004),
Academic Free License version 1.1, "found in file LICENSE". This repository
does not include that AFL 1.1 text. The root `LICENSE` covers the original
work in section 1; `kdtree2.f90` keeps the notice in its own header.

A detailed description of each change, with the upstream defect it addresses, is in
[`docs/SOLVER-PATCHES.md`](docs/SOLVER-PATCHES.md).

**To rebuild from unmodified upstream sources**, point the build at your own checkout
of `Image_Velocimetry_Solver/sources/` and expect to run in P2 mode (`--no-pgm-binary`),
which is roughly 59× slower.

